WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.479
Words with a faint dotted underline can be tapped.

00:00:03.479 --> 00:00:09.737
You'll see the original Hebrew or Greek word, what it means, and where else it appears in Scripture.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.047
To mark a passage, tap a verse number.

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:18.721
Tap more numbers to select several verses together, and then choose a highlight color.

00:00:18.721 --> 00:00:21.228
You can copy the verses from here too.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.657
From the same bar, you can write a note, or start a journal entry about those verses.

00:00:27.657 --> 00:00:30.371
Type it, or tap the microphone and speak.

00:00:31.172 --> 00:00:39.981
The Study tab opens at the verse you're reading, with commentaries from Matthew Henry, Calvin, Gill, Spurgeon's sermons, and more.

00:00:39.981 --> 00:00:46.553
Swipe left or right for the next commentary, or tap the round button in the corner to choose one.

00:00:47.355 --> 00:00:58.745
Back in the Bible, a small question mark under a verse number means there's more to see: a prophecy of Christ with its passages, or the places named, with a photo and a map.

00:00:58.745 --> 00:01:04.144
The one by each chapter title shows where that chapter fits in the book's outline.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:11.135
Maps and Helps has maps for every chapter, the journeys of Jesus and of Paul, and much more.

00:01:11.135 --> 00:01:16.362
Tap the corner button to see a map full screen, and tap it again to come back.
